## 1. Project Overview

This project presents a comprehensive Governance, Risk and Compliance (GRC) assessment and Information Security Management System (ISMS) improvement proposal for NovaPay Financial Services, a growing digital payments and mobile banking business operating across West and Southern Africa.

The assessment examines information security governance, financial data protection, third-party risk, regulatory obligations, and operational resilience.

The primary objective is to develop a structured, risk-based approach that strengthens NovaPay's security governance and supports alignment with ISO/IEC 27001:2022 and other applicable frameworks.

The project demonstrates practical GRC competencies through the development of security policies, risk assessments, treatment plans, an ISO 27001 Statement of Applicability, and a phased implementation roadmap.

> **Project scope:** This is an academic, document-based case study. The findings, risk scores, recommendations, and proposed controls do not represent a verified operational audit or ISO certification.

