## 10. Third-Party and Supplier Risk Management

Third-party governance is a major focus of the assessment because NovaPay relies on external partners for payment processing, banking integration, cloud services and other business-critical functions.

### Supplier Risk Classification

| Supplier Tier | Risk Characteristics | Proposed Oversight |
|---|---|---|
| High / Critical | Sensitive data, privileged access or critical payment services | Pre-onboarding security assessment, quarterly reviews and annual reassessment |
| Medium | Limited confidential information or non-critical restricted integration | Proportionate assessment and annual review |
| Low | No sensitive access and limited service dependency | Basic due diligence and change-triggered review |

### Supplier Security Lifecycle

The proposed lifecycle includes:

1. Supplier identification and registration.
2. Business ownership assignment.
3. Security and privacy due diligence.
4. Risk classification.
5. Contractual security requirements.
6. Approved technical access.
7. Ongoing monitoring and reassessment.
8. Secure offboarding and credential revocation.

The supplier security policy also addresses concentration risk, incident cooperation, data transfers, subcontractors and business continuity.

