## 11. Proposed 90-Day Implementation Roadmap

The assessment translates identified risks into a phased implementation plan.

| Phase | Timeline | Key Activities |
|---|---|---|
| Establish Control | Days 1–15 | Assign accountable roles, inventory integrations and escalate critical exposures |
| Establish Baseline | Days 16–30 | Approve risk methodology, review access, map data flows and develop governance records |
| Implement | Days 31–60 | Conduct supplier assessments, implement policy awareness and exercise incident response |
| Verify | Days 61–90 | Test recovery arrangements, verify remediation and review residual risks |
| Maintain | After Day 90 | Continue management reviews, risk reassessment and independent assurance |

### Proposed Performance Indicators

The roadmap includes measurable targets such as:

- 100% of active partner integrations assigned an owner and approved scope by day 30.
- 100% of operating countries assigned compliance obligation owners by day 30.
- 100% of high-risk suppliers assessed and tracked by day 60.
- At least 95% security training completion by day 60.
- Critical service recovery scenarios tested by day 90.

These are proposed targets rather than verified achievements.

